2:00 – 2:30 | Mini‑Project: Unit Converter

Task: Build a program that converts:

· Miles to Kilometers (1 mile = 1.60934 km)
· Pounds to Kilograms (1 pound = 0.453592 kg)

Code skeleton (with menu):

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int choice;
    double value, result;
    cout << "1. Miles to Kilometers\n";
    cout << "2. Pounds to Kilograms\n";
    cout << "Choose: ";
    cin >> choice;
    cout << "Enter value: ";
    cin >> value;

    if (choice == 1) {
        result = value * 1.60934;
        cout << value << " miles = " << result << " km" << endl;
    } else if (choice == 2) {
        result = value * 0.453592;
        cout << value << " pounds = " << result << " kg" << endl;
    } else {
        cout << "Invalid choice" << endl;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

Challenge: Add more conversions (e.g., Celsius ↔ Fahrenheit, inches ↔ cm).

